{
 "date": "Tuesday, October 13, 2026",
 "top_story": {
  "eyebrow": "Top Story",
  "headline": "Rep. Gilbert Cisneros discloses 57 trades in a month, 31 of them on two days",
  "dek": "The periodic transaction report covers stocks plus three bond lines of $250,001 to $500,000 each.",
  "paragraphs": [
   "<strong>Rep. Gilbert Cisneros</strong> (D-CA31) filed a periodic transaction report on October 12 listing 57 transactions dated September 3 through October 1, 2026: 29 purchases, 10 full sales, 17 partial sales and one exchange. Thirteen trades are dated September 18 and 18 are dated September 29. <a href=\"https://disclosures-clerk.house.gov/public_disc/ptr-pdfs/2026/20035622.pdf\">Filing</a>.",
   "The largest lines are municipal bonds: a purchase and a partial sale of <strong>California Community Choice Financing Authority</strong> revenue bonds and a purchase of <strong>Indiana Finance Authority</strong> health system revenue bonds, each $250,001 to $500,000. He also sold <strong>El Camino Community College District</strong> and <strong>Imperial Irrigation District</strong> bonds in the $100,001 to $250,000 range. The equity trades are mostly $1,001 to $15,000 and include semiconductor names (<strong>NXP Semiconductors</strong>, <strong>ON Semiconductor</strong>, <strong>Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company</strong>, <strong>MACOM Technology Solutions</strong>) and <strong>WuXi AppTec</strong>. The input flags none of the trades as late."
  ],
  "callout": {
   "label": "Read the filings",
   "links": [
    {
     "text": "Cisneros periodic transaction report",
     "url": "https://disclosures-clerk.house.gov/public_disc/ptr-pdfs/2026/20035622.pdf"
    }
   ]
  }
 },
